---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import FAQ from "../components/FAQ.astro";
const title = "FAQs";
import "../styles.css";
---

<style>
  h1 {
    text-align: center;
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin: 2rem 1rem 0rem 1rem;
    font-weight: bold;
    font-size: larger;
  }

  h2 {
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0.75rem 0;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--color-accent);
    padding-bottom: 0.3rem;
  }

  .faq-sections {
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .faq-container {
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }
</style>

<BaseLayout title={title}>
  <h1>Frequently Asked Questions</h1>

  <div class="faq-sections">
    <h2>Mining</h2>
    <div class="faq-container">
      <FAQ question="What is the algorithm used in this project?">
        The new algorithm is called "Janushash". More detailed information can
        be found <a href="https://docs.warthog.network/unique-features/janushash/">here</a>.
      </FAQ>

      <FAQ question="Can I run mining on a GPU or CPU only?">
        No, you can't. The Miner uses both GPU and CPU.
      </FAQ>

      <FAQ question="Where can I find the latest releases of the node, wallet, and miner?">
        You can find precompiled binaries of Node and Wallet: <a
          href="https://docs.warthog.network/guides/node/">here</a
        >.<br />
        Miner (Linux and HiveOS builds): <a
          href="https://docs.warthog.network/guides/mining/quickstart/"
          >here</a
        >.<br />
        See README.md in these repos for usage information.
      </FAQ>

      <FAQ question="I'm getting this error in the miner output: [error] API request failed. Are you running the node with RPC endpoint enabled? [warning] Could not get mining information, retrying in 100 milliseconds...">
        You should run the node with <code>--rpc=0.0.0.0:3000</code> to accept remote
        connections from your rigs and prevent this error. Keep in mind that you can
        only run one node per public IP.
      </FAQ>

      <FAQ question="The Miner exits with error 'custom exiter (exitcode=0), waiting to cooldown a bit'">
        Most likely your CPU is too old. The CPU must support these
        instructions: <code
          >'-mpclmul', '-msse4', '-msse4.1', '-msse4.2', '-mssse3', '-mavx',
          '-maes'</code
        >
      </FAQ>

      <FAQ question='What does "CPU queue full" and "CPU queue drained" mean?'>
        It means that there is an imbalance between CPU and GPU, this can happen
        sometimes but should not occur often. CPU queue drained can happen more
        often and is normal on each new block height. It should rebalance itself
        independent of how many threads you choose. Just look at the CPU load.
        If it is as specified everything is good. For example if you specify two
        threads two processor threads should be in use close to 100% . If that
        happens most of the time, everything is good.
      </FAQ>

      <FAQ question='What does "CPU outruns GPU" mean?'>
        GPU and CPU compute different hash functions so it can happen if the GPU
        is slow and the CPU fast.
      </FAQ>
    </div>

    <h2>Node</h2>
    <div class="faq-container">
      <FAQ question="My node is stuck and won't sync?">
        Make sure you are running the latest version <code
          >wart-node-linux --version</code
        >. Delete folder with node db files and start the node again. (It
        locates in home directory <code>~/.warthog</code> if you are using Linux and
        <code>%AppData%\Local\Warthog</code> in Windows)
      </FAQ>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>